 GALACTOSA:Los niveles de galactosa libre plasmática son un indicador clave en el diagnóstico de galactosemia clásica.", "NIVEL DE GAL-1-P:NIVEL DE GAL-1-P is a significant marker in the diagnosis and management of classic galactosemia. The levels of Gal-1-P in erythrocytes serve as an important indicator for diagnosing this condition. Additionally, monitoring the level of Gal-1-P is crucial for assessing the effectiveness of dietary restrictions in individuals affected by galactosemia.", "DIAGNÓSTICO:The entity \"DIAGNÓSTICO\" encompasses various processes related to the identification of medical conditions and diseases. Diagnosis of fructan intolerance typically involves dietary elimination and monitoring symptom improvement. In the context of inflammatory bowel disease, diagnosis is essential for effective management. Additionally, \"diagnóstico\" refers to identifying elevated homocysteine levels, which is often done through plasma concentration tests. It also includes the identification of urea cycle disorders through biochemical tests and enzyme activity measurements. In the realm of food allergies and intolerances, diagnosis involves pinpointing the cause of symptoms through testing and ruling out other disorders. Furthermore, early diagnosis of classic galactosemia is critical to prevent complications. Overall, \"DIAGNÓSTICO\" represents a comprehensive approach to identifying various health conditions through specific testing and assessment methods.", "Β-CETOGALACTÓNICO:β-Cetogalactónico es un metabolito en la vía de metabolización de la galactosa.", "XILULOSA:Xilulosa es un metabolito que se forma en la vía de las pentosas fosfato, relacionada con el metabolismo de la galactosa.", "VÍA DE LAS PENTOSAS FOSFATO:La vía de las pentosas fosfato es una ruta metabólica que genera intermediarios importantes en el metabolismo de carbohidratos, incluyendo galactosa.", "GALACTOSA-1-FOSFATO:Galactosa-1-fosfato es un metabolito que se forma en el metabolismo de la galactosa y es crucial para su conversión a glucosa.", "UDP-GALACTOSA:UDP-galactosa es un nucleótido que se forma en el metabolismo de la galactosa y es importante para la síntesis de macromoléculas glicosiladas.", "PIRUVATO:Piruvato, also known as pyruvate, is a final metabolite in the glycolysis process, generated from glucose. It is also associated with the metabolism of galactose. Additionally, pyruvate is recognized for its potential benefits in enhancing energy production, particularly among athletes who may utilize it to improve their performance.", "MACROMOLÉCULAS GLICOSILADAS:Las macromoléculas glicosiladas son compuestos que se forman a partir de la unión de azúcares, incluyendo galactosa, y son importantes en la biología celular.", "GALACTOLÍPIDOS:Galactolípidos are lipids that contain galactose, playing a significant role in the context of metabolic disorders associated with galactose. Additionally, they are essential components of cellular membranes, highlighting their importance in both metabolic processes and structural integrity within cells.", "GALACTOPROTEÍNAS:Las galactoproteínas son proteínas que contienen galactosa y desempeñan roles importantes en diversas funciones biológicas.) <|COMPLETE|>"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}